{"genre": "Essay", "passage_A": "Heart disease, cancer, and diabetes are among the top killers globally. Genetics and other factors play roles, but studies indicate that adopting a healthy diet can substantially lower the risk of these conditions. Organizations such as the American Heart Association, American Cancer Society, and American Diabetes Association offer dietary guidelines aimed at preventing heart disease, cancer, and diabetes.

For heart health, the American Heart Association suggests cutting back on saturated and trans fats, sodium, added sugars, and processed meats. Instead, they advocate for a diet rich in fruits, vegetables, whole grains, lean proteins, and healthy fats like nuts, seeds, avocado, and olive oil. They also recommend moderating alcohol consumption and boosting physical activity.

The American Cancer Society recommends a diet heavy in plant-based foods such as fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and legumes.", "passage_B": "Heart disease, cancer and diabetes are the three leading causes of death in the world. Although there are many factors that can cause these diseases, research has shown that a healthy diet can significantly reduce the risk of developing these diseases. The American Heart Association recommends a diet low in saturated fats, trans fats, sodium, added sugars and processed meats, and high in fruits, vegetables, whole grains, lean meats and healthy fats such as nuts, seeds, avocados and olive oil, and low in alcohol and high in physical activity. The American Cancer Society recommends a diet high in fruits, vegetables, whole grains and legumes."}

